---
import MainLayout from "../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout
  title="Springs Fire in Moreno Valley Burns Over 4,000 Acres, Evacuations Underway"
  description="The Springs Fire in Moreno Valley has burned over 4,000 acres and is threatening homes, with evacuation orders and road closures in place."
  canonical="https://www.stayjustin.com/west-covina-news/moreno-valley-brush-fire-evacuations/"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container intro-block">
      <h1>Springs Fire Burns Thousands of Acres in Moreno Valley, Evacuations Underway</h1>

      <p class="intro-copy">
        A fast-moving brush fire in Moreno Valley has burned more than 4,100 acres and is threatening homes,
        with evacuation orders issued as crews work to contain the blaze.
      </p>

      <p class="intro-copy">
        The Springs Fire was first reported around 10:59 a.m. near Gilman Springs Road and continues to grow
        under strong Santa Ana wind conditions.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CURRENT STATUS -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container intro-block">
      <h2 class="section-title">Current Situation</h2>

      <p class="intro-copy">
        As of the evening update, the fire has burned approximately 4,176 acres and is about 10% contained.
      </p>

      <p class="intro-copy">
        The fire has spread past Gilman Hot Springs, crossed Davis Road, and is now burning near areas north of Lake Perris,
        where campgrounds and nearby properties are at risk.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- EVACUATIONS -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container intro-block">
      <h2 class="section-title">Evacuations and Closures</h2>

      <p class="intro-copy">
        Evacuation orders have been issued in multiple zones, with additional areas under warning as conditions change.
      </p>

      <p class="intro-copy">
        Major road closures include:
        <br /><br />
        • Gilman Springs Rd / Alessandro Blvd<br />
        • Alessandro Rd / Redlands Blvd<br />
        • Bridge Rd / Gilman Springs Rd<br />
        • Ramona Expressway / Davis Rd
      </p>

      <p class="intro-copy">
        A temporary evacuation shelter has been opened at Valley View High School in Moreno Valley.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- RESPONSE -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container intro-block">
      <h2 class="section-title">Fire Response</h2>

      <p class="intro-copy">
        Fire crews are actively working to contain the blaze using ground crews, bulldozers,
        and aerial support including helicopters and air tankers dropping water and fire retardant.
      </p>

      <p class="intro-copy">
        Strong winds are continuing to fuel the fire, making containment efforts more difficult.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECOND FIRE -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container intro-block">
      <h2 class="section-title">Additional Fire in Los Angeles County</h2>

      <p class="intro-copy">
        At the same time, crews in Los Angeles County are responding to a separate brush fire near Soledad Canyon Road.
      </p>

      <p class="intro-copy">
        That fire has burned around 280 acres and is only partially contained, with evacuation concerns reported.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHY IT MATTERS -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container intro-block">
      <h2 class="section-title">Why This Matters for West Covina Residents</h2>

      <p class="intro-copy">
        While Moreno Valley is roughly 45 miles away, fires of this size can impact air quality across the region
        and may require shared emergency resources from surrounding departments.
      </p>

      <p class="intro-copy">
        These events also highlight how quickly fire conditions can escalate across Southern California during high wind conditions.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- RELATED -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container intro-block">
      <h2 class="section-title">Related Coverage</h2>

      <p class="intro-copy">
        <a href="/west-covina-news/">All West Covina news</a><br />
        <a href="/city-hall/">West Covina City Hall updates</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</MainLayout>
